# Which registered agents get an executor process, and which of those processes
# share a container. Copy to fleet.yaml and edit.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING AN AGENT.
#
# 1. This file declares intent; `agent_runtimes` records fact. Generating
#    containers from the table instead would be circular: the row records where
#    a process is, so a process started from the row cannot be what created it,
#    and a stale row would perpetuate itself. `agent-control-fleet doctor`
#    is the reconciliation between the two, and it fixes nothing.
#
# 2. One agent is one process. The SDK holds a single agent per process and the
#    ADK plugin refuses to initialize under a second name. That constraint binds
#    a process, not a container: a group is one container running one
#    `adk api_server` per agent listed in it, each on its own port from 8000 and
#    with its own agents directory. Nothing publishes a host port: the executor's
#    HTTP API has no authentication of its own, and the only real control is that
#    its port is reachable from the server's network and nowhere else.
#
# 3. A group is a trust boundary. Its members share a network namespace, a PID
#    namespace and a tmpfs, so an injected sibling reaches the network any
#    web-enabled process in the group reaches and can read its environment. That
#    is why `web_tools` may not differ inside one group; splitting the group in
#    two is the fix and it is one line. On this runtime a container costs about
#    2GB, so grouping is also what the fleet's memory bill is made of.
#
# 4. `agent_name` is also a directory name inside the container. ADK routes on
#    the folder, not on App(name=...), so the name must be lowercase letters,
#    digits and underscores. A hyphen or a colon is accepted by the server and
#    unroutable as an app, which surfaces as a 500 on the first turn rather than
#    as anything an operator can read. A group name may also carry hyphens; it
#    becomes the container name, with underscores translated.
#
# 5. `web_tools` is the Exa toolset, on by default. An agent with an outbound
#    fetch tool is an SSRF pivot onto the network its own executor sits on, and
#    with company knowledge also on it is a retrieval-plus-egress pair. Turning
#    both on is a decision; see docs/plans/agent-fleet-topology.md section 3.2.
#
# The model base URL is NOT configured here. It is computed from the live
# network gateway at `up` time, because the gateway is what the host is from
# inside these VMs and host.docker.internal resolves to nothing on this runtime.
# AGENT_CONTROL_FLEET_MODEL_BASE_URL overrides it and refuses a loopback address.
#
# Resources are environment too, and they are per container rather than per
# agent. The runtime default is 1024MB and 4 CPUs apiece; the fleet asks for
# 512MB and 2 CPUs instead, against a process measured at 37MB idle and 105MB
# through a turn with a tool call. AGENT_CONTROL_FLEET_EXECUTOR_MEMORY and
# AGENT_CONTROL_FLEET_EXECUTOR_CPUS override that, and a group of four wants
# more than a group of one.
#
# Credentials are environment, not file: AGENT_CONTROL_FLEET_REGISTER_API_KEY is
# the admin key the two one-shot jobs hold, and AGENT_CONTROL_FLEET_EXECUTOR_API_KEY
# is the key every executor runs on. `up` refuses to start anything when the
# second cannot reach the halt path, because an executor that cannot has lost the
# operator STOP button while the console still shows the halt recorded.

version: 1
image: agent-control-executor:local

defaults:
  web_tools: true

# Adding an agent is a reviewed decision about a container that runs
# model-driven code. Keep this list to agents somebody is actually using.
#
# One agent per group is the per-agent topology: a container each, and the
# strongest isolation the runtime offers. Listing two in one group trades that
# isolation for about 2GB, and is only sound when they are already peers.
groups:
  - name: marketing
    agents:
      - agent_name: marketing_researcher
      - agent_name: marketing_copywriter

  # Its own group rather than a third member of marketing: egress may not differ
  # inside a group, and this agent is the one that should not have it.
  - name: sales
    agents:
      - agent_name: sales_outreach_drafter
        web_tools: false
